# Jettison environment template.
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in real values from your Supabase project
# dashboard (Project Settings -> API Keys). Never commit real values;
# .env.local is gitignored.
#
# Naming follows Supabase's new API-key system:
#   - sb_publishable_*  (public, safe in browser)  -> replaces "anon key"
#   - sb_secret_*       (server-only, RLS-bypass)  -> replaces "service_role key"

# --- Public (browser-visible) ---------------------------------------------
# These are inlined into the client bundle by Next.js. The publishable key
# is intentionally public; RLS in Postgres is the protection. Do NOT put
# anything secret behind a NEXT_PUBLIC_* name -- the prefix means "ship to
# every browser visitor".

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# --- Server-only ----------------------------------------------------------
# Secret key bypasses RLS. Server modules only. NEVER prefix with
# NEXT_PUBLIC_, NEVER imported from a "use client" file or any module
# reachable from one. See .cursor/rules/typescript-react.mdc for the hard
# rule and the rg boundary check.

# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
